WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:05.957
- I'm excited to try on her dress.

00:00:05.957 --> 00:00:08.883
I never really thought
that I would ever wear it.

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:10.590
- You know what, I really
don't know what to expect.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.598
- I'm probably not going to get emotional.

00:00:12.598 --> 00:00:13.550
Sorry about that!

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.258
- No, it's okay!

00:00:14.258 --> 00:00:15.060
- I might cry.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:15.756
But I might not.

00:00:15.756 --> 00:00:16.302
- Oh God!

00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:17.718
- I'm definitely gonna cry.

00:00:20.118 --> 00:00:21.689
- It was a nice dress for $25.

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:23.895
- It'd be like a $40 dress today, right?

00:00:23.895 --> 00:00:26.135
- My mother in law wore it in 1952,

00:00:26.135 --> 00:00:28.759
and then I wore it in 1987.

00:00:28.759 --> 00:00:31.325
And so, this'll be the third time

00:00:31.325 --> 00:00:33.368
it's been put on by
somebody in our family.

00:00:33.368 --> 00:00:36.828
- This dress was meant to be a symbol

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:41.623
of dreams and hopes and
what I wanted for my life.

00:00:42.914 --> 00:00:44.833
- [Blonde Girl] So Mother, turn around.

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:46.122
- Okay, you can turn around now.

00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:48.049
- Turn around Mama.

00:00:48.049 --> 00:00:50.336
- (gasps) Oh my God!

00:00:50.336 --> 00:00:52.170
- [Daughter] (laughs) Mama...

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.516
I look like you.

00:00:54.516 --> 00:00:57.302
- (laughs) The sleeves!

00:00:57.302 --> 00:00:59.427
- Your arms are longer than mine.

00:00:59.427 --> 00:01:00.553
- Well, I think you look great.

00:01:00.553 --> 00:01:02.643
- I feel like Keira Knightley.

00:01:02.643 --> 00:01:03.513
In a good way!

00:01:03.513 --> 00:01:04.558
There is nothing bad, ever,

00:01:04.558 --> 00:01:05.975
about feeling like Keira Knightley.

00:01:05.975 --> 00:01:08.889
I just feel like this
looks like the nightgown

00:01:08.889 --> 00:01:12.151
of a queen in the 1700's.

00:01:12.151 --> 00:01:13.858
- Obviously, it doesn't fit

00:01:13.858 --> 00:01:15.530
so I couldn't wear it.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.283
I could just go like this right now

00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:19.477
and just bust the whole thing open.

00:01:20.553 --> 00:01:22.073
I do think it's really pretty.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:24.536
- Oh, Mom.

00:01:24.536 --> 00:01:27.833
I used to idolize my mom when I was a kid

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:30.376
and I just remember
her looking so gorgeous

00:01:30.376 --> 00:01:33.336
like a Barbie, so it's really
interesting to be in this.

00:01:33.336 --> 00:01:34.885
I never thought that I'd wear it.

00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:37.922
- I think it's a really nice dress.

00:01:37.922 --> 00:01:39.385
- It is a really nice dress.

00:01:39.385 --> 00:01:41.928
- There wasn't a Lifetime
movie moment here,

00:01:41.928 --> 00:01:43.182
no one cried.

00:01:43.182 --> 00:01:44.145
- No, no one cried.

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:45.980
- So when are you gonna get married?

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.141
- (laughs) Nice try, Mom.

00:01:47.141 --> 00:01:47.849
(laughs)

00:01:47.849 --> 00:01:49.312
- It was very emotional for me

00:01:49.312 --> 00:01:52.528
just to think that she
might try on my dress

00:01:52.528 --> 00:01:55.140
and it was just nerve-wracking to think

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.742
of this step in her life.

00:01:56.742 --> 00:01:57.868
- Oh, Oh my God!

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:58.611
- Mom!

00:01:58.611 --> 00:02:00.330
- If it would have fit me perfectly

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.083
I think it might have been
a different experience,

00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:04.869
like, "Oh, I could see myself
walking down the aisle!"

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:08.166
But this is more like I'm playing dress up

00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:10.035
when I'm ten years old, or something.

00:02:10.035 --> 00:02:11.626
- I expect to see you in a dress like this

00:02:11.626 --> 00:02:13.333
maybe when I'm in a nursing home.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.132
- That's upsetting.

00:02:17.132 --> 00:02:18.302
- I don't think that's a question!

00:02:18.302 --> 00:02:19.010
(laughs)

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.217
- I think that you wear it best.

00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:20.810
- Yeah?

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:21.971
- You do, yeah.

00:02:21.971 --> 00:02:22.725
- I actually think you did,

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:25.012
'cause I think that the hat makes it.

00:02:25.012 --> 00:02:27.392
- Oh, my mom totally wore it better.

00:02:27.392 --> 00:02:29.099
My mom, for sure.

00:02:29.099 --> 00:02:30.144
- No...

00:02:30.144 --> 00:02:31.235
- She is so gorgeous.

00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:32.396
- She totally wore it.

00:02:32.396 --> 00:02:33.650
- No, I think she did.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:35.775
- [Mom] When I saw you with the veil on,

00:02:35.775 --> 00:02:36.982
it was actually kind of funny!

00:02:36.982 --> 00:02:37.992
(laughs)

00:02:37.992 --> 00:02:38.851
- [Daughter] Oh yeah, the
veil made me look like the

00:02:38.851 --> 00:02:41.278
- [Both] Bride of Frankenstein!

00:02:41.278 --> 00:02:43.031
- That's what I thought
when I first saw you

00:02:43.031 --> 00:02:44.146
but I didn't want to say that

00:02:44.146 --> 00:02:45.190
because I didn't want to offend you,

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:45.627
but yeah.

